This is mainly a simulation library of xilinx primitives that are
verilator compatible.

UltraScale+
-----------
The models simulate Vivado funcsim netlists (write_verilog -mode funcsim) of UltraScale+
designs in Verilator:

    verilator --cc --no-timing -DGLBL -Wno-fatal -y <this directory> --top-module <top> netlist.v

-DGLBL skips the netlist's own glbl module.  Covered: LUT1-6, FDRE, FDSE (with the
IS_*_INVERTED attributes), CARRY8, MUXF7, MUXF8, SRL16E, SRLC32E, RAM32X1D, RAM32M, RAM32M16,
RAM64M8, DSP48E2, BUFGCE (as a gate), RAMB18E2/RAMB36E2 (full-width true dual port, written by
gen_ramb.py) and URAM288 (stand-alone and cascaded).  The block RAM and UltraRAM models stop at
elaboration on configurations they do not model.

test/netdiff/netdiff.py checks the models against Vivado's unisims on the primitive instances of
a funcsim netlist (random stimulus, xsim against Verilator, every output every cycle);
test/netdiff/example/example.tcl writes a small one:

    source <Vivado>/settings64.sh
    vivado -mode batch -source test/netdiff/example/example.tcl -tclargs work/example_funcsim.v
    test/netdiff/netdiff.py work/example_funcsim.v work --per 8 --cycles 20000 [--pool 0]

test/uram288/run.sh checks URAM288 against the unisim in xsim, stand-alone and in 2- and 3-deep
cascades.

CARRY8, MUXF7, MUXF8, SRLC32E, RAM32M, RAM32M16, RAM64M8, LUT1-6, FDRE and FDSE are from
fredrequin/verilator_xilinx (BSD license, Copyright (c) 2019-2022 Frederic Requin).
